From d7b5cc6a6c54745e980663bba95dd031d4bbbd0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Parimalarengan Gururajan <gururaja@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 19:49:02 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] dpp: support live BSS reconfiguration via Reconfiguration
 Trigger

Add end-to-end support for the EasyMesh DPP Reconfiguration Trigger flow,
so a controller can push updated SSID/credentials to an already-onboarded
DPP agent, not just during initial onboarding.

Agent: handle RECONFIGURATION_TRIGGER_MESSAGE and apply the resulting BSS
Configuration Response to already-CONFIGURED radios; fix the FSM re-arming
and reset-suppression bugs that made this only work on the first attempt.

Controller: send the trigger to DPP-onboarded agents on config changes,
scope BSS Configuration Response entries per-radio, and handle re-chirp/
re-search from already-onboarded agents as a clean restart.

Signed-off-by: Parimalarengan Gururajan <gururaja@qti.qualcomm.com>
